  "term": "BDNF",
  "definition": "BDNF, or brain-derived neurotrophic factor, is a trophic protein in the nerve growth factor family. It supports certain brain neurons, including retinal, cholinergic, and dopaminergic cells, and also affects motor and sensory neurons in the peripheral nervous system.",
